WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W9 (0.1.3)


STATE

  Version 0.1.3, Phase P2 (POSIX shell options), on branch dev.
  It adds:
  - shared option module (include/tam-clam/options.h, src/options.c)
    supporting -a/allexport, -C/noclobber, -e/errexit, -f/noglob,
    -n/noexec, -u/nounset, -x/xtrace, and -o pipefail (POSIX.1-2024),
    with set -o / set +o output and $- flags;
  - CLI option parsing in src/main.c (-/+ flags, clustered flags like
    -euc and -es, -o/+o named options, and -n parse-only mode);
  - set -e (errexit) in src/exec.c following POSIX.1-2024 rules
    (ignored in if/elif/while/until conditions, non-last &&/||, negated
    ! pipelines, and non-subshell compound commands; active in
    subshells, functions, pipelines, and assignment command subs; EXIT
    traps still run with the failing status);
  - set -u (nounset) in src/expand.c and src/arith.c (exempting
    @/*/#/?/-/$/!/0, default/alt/assign forms, and short-circuited
    arithmetic branches);
  - set -o pipefail in src/exec.c (rightmost non-zero pipeline status);
  - set -x (xtrace) in src/exec.c with PS4 expansion (reusing
    tc_lex_expand_parts), LINENO tracking, and shell-quoted arguments;
  - set -C (noclobber) in src/exec.c with O_EXCL, >| override, and
    non-regular file allowance (/dev/null, FIFOs);
  - set -n (noexec) parse-only syntax checking in main.c and exec.c
    (ignored when interactive);
  - sandbox/demo-0.1.3-options added to sandbox/play.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0; FUNCNEST sets the function recursion limit; signed
  64-bit arithmetic overflow is a reported error; echo recognizes -n only
  and does not interpret backslash escapes by default.


